        <h2>Conventions</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>CSV and Parquet carry the same 44 columns in the same order, for the per-country, ALL, EDU and GOV packages. New columns are only ever appended at the end, so reading by position keeps working.</li>
          <li>CSV is all text. In Parquet every column is text except <code>Latitude</code> and <code>Longitude</code> (double) and <code>AccuracyRadius</code> and <code>CityGeonameId</code> (int32).</li>
          <li>Yes/no columns hold <code>Y</code> or <code>N</code>.</li>
          <li><em>When absent</em> says what a missing value looks like: <code>-</code> (a literal dash), null (an empty CSV cell), or never empty.</li>
          <li>The MMDB file holds one record per network with 42 of these fields. The network itself is the lookup key, so <code>IP24Prefix</code> is not stored, and <code>AccuracyRadius</code> is not included.</li>
          <li>The BOG (bogon) package uses a reduced schema: <code>snapshot_month</code>, <code>IP24Prefix</code>, <code>BogonType</code>, <code>IsCoreBogon</code>, <code>IsSecurityOverlay</code>, <code>RIR</code>, <code>RIRStatus</code>.</li>
        </ul>

